The audit found the root cause: the developer message's "Available tools" + "Guidelines" block (~900-1000 chars) duplicates info already in each tool's `description` inside `tools[]`. The model gets the same guidance twice — once compact, once verbose. Combined with trimming `memory_search` and `session_search` descriptions, we can recover ~550-650 tokens (~33-39%) from the 1677-token baseline without touching the context limit. Note: the schemas live in `pi-hermes-memory`, not this repo, so trimming them means editing that project.
